ALTER TABLE categories ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_html TEXT;

UPDATE categories
SET content_html = '<h2>3 Seater Sofa Collection</h2>
<p>A 3 seater sofa is the piece most Pakistani living rooms are actually built around. It anchors the room before anything else gets arranged, which means getting the size, frame, and fabric right matters more here than on almost any other piece of furniture in the house. This collection is built on that principle: every 3 seater sofa is made to order at our workshop in Lahore, cut and upholstered after you confirm the design, not pulled from a warehouse shelf.</p>
<h2>What Makes a 3 Seater Sofa Worth the Investment</h2>
<p>Most 3 seater sofa designs in Pakistan are judged by their fabric and silhouette, and almost never by what holds the piece together underneath. We build every frame from solid wood, backed by a 2.5-year warranty, so the joints stay tight instead of loosening after a few years of daily sitting and standing. The seat and back cushions use Molty Foam, carrying a 5-year warranty, which keeps its shape through years of regular use instead of compressing flat within months the way unbranded foam often does.</p>
<p>This matters because a 3 seater sofa typically gets more daily contact than any other seat in the house. It is where guests sit first, where the family gathers in the evening, and where the wear shows fastest if the foam and frame are not built for it.</p>
<h2>Designs and Dimensions in This Collection</h2>
<p>The collection spans the styles Pakistani buyers search for most: curved and boucle-finished pieces for contemporary living rooms, channel tufted and chesterfield-leaning designs for more formal drawing rooms, and L shape configurations for corner placement where an open floor plan calls for it. Each product page lists exact dimensions, since 3 seater sofa size in feet varies more than most buyers expect. A standard 3 seater typically runs close to 6 to 7 feet in width, but the depth, arm style, and back height shift the footprint enough that measuring your space before ordering is worth the extra five minutes.</p>
<p>If you are comparing a 3 seater sofa price in Pakistan across different sellers, the dimensions are usually where the real difference in value sits. A wider, deeper sofa built on solid wood will outlast a narrower one built on a lighter frame, even if the listed price looks similar.</p>
<h2>Choosing the Right 3 Seater for Your Room</h2>
<p>A 3 seater sofa works best as the main seating piece in a small to medium living room, or as one part of a larger arrangement alongside a 2 seater or armchairs in bigger spaces. If your room is on the smaller side, look at the curved and lower-arm designs in this collection rather than boxy chesterfield silhouettes, since the visual weight of a sofa changes how a room reads even when the floor footprint is similar. For larger drawing rooms, the channel tufted and wood frame designs hold their presence better against high ceilings and bigger walls.</p>
<p>Fabric choice also affects daily life more than buyers usually plan for. Boucle and chenille resist visible wear well in dusty environments and stay comfortable through Lahore summers, while velvet adds a more formal look but shows pile marks if not brushed occasionally. We can talk you through which fabric suits your household over WhatsApp before you commit to a colour.</p>
<h2>Pairing a 3 Seater Sofa with the Rest of the Room</h2>
<p>A 3 seater sofa rarely sits alone in a Pakistani drawing room. It is usually paired with a 2 seater, a pair of accent chairs, or built up into a larger 5 seater or 7 seater arrangement over time as the household grows or the room gets reorganised. If you are buying with that future arrangement in mind, it is worth checking that the frame height, arm style, and fabric of your 3 seater will still sit comfortably alongside other pieces you might add later, rather than choosing it purely in isolation. Several designs in this collection share consistent leg styles and fabric ranges with our 2 seater sofas specifically so the two can be matched without a visible mismatch.</p>
<h2>Ordering a 3 Seater Sofa from ComfyClub</h2>
<p>Every order starts with choosing your design and fabric colour, confirmed directly with us over WhatsApp. Production begins once 60 percent of the price is paid in advance, with the remaining 40 percent due before delivery. A 3 seater sofa typically takes 20 to 25 working days to craft and deliver from our Lahore workshop, and we ship across Pakistan, not only within the city.</p>
<p>If you are unsure which design or size fits your space, send us your room dimensions before ordering. We would rather help you choose the right 3 seater sofa once than have you order the wrong size and live with it for years.</p>'
WHERE slug = '/seater-sofas/3-seater-sofas/' OR name ILIKE '3 Seater%';

UPDATE categories
SET content_html = '<h2>4 Seater Sofa Collection</h2>
<p>A 4 seater sofa sits in the space between a standard 3 seater and a full sectional, wide enough to seat a family comfortably without committing to an L shape or modular layout. It is a less common size in Pakistani furniture shopping than 3 seater or 5 seater sofa sets, which is exactly why getting it right matters: there are fewer reference points to compare against, so the design and build quality carry more weight in the decision. Every 4 seater sofa in this collection is made to order at our workshop in Lahore.</p>
<h2>Why a 4 Seater Sofa Suits Certain Rooms Better Than a Set</h2>
<p>A 5 seater or 6 seater sofa set usually comes as multiple pieces, a 3 seater plus a loveseat or armchairs, arranged around a room. A 4 seater sofa is one continuous piece instead, which works better in living rooms where you want generous seating without breaking it into separate furniture items. It also suits households who entertain in smaller groups but still want enough width for four people to sit without crowding, or families who prefer one long sofa against a wall over a scattered arrangement.</p>
<p>A 4 seater sofa price in Pakistan is usually harder to compare than a 3 seater or 5 seater, simply because fewer sellers stock this size, so buyers have less to benchmark against. The frame and foam matter just as much here as on any other size. We build every 4 seater sofa on a solid wood frame with a 2.5-year warranty, so the extra width does not translate into extra strain on weak joints. The cushioning uses Molty Foam with a 5-year warranty, holding its shape across the full seat length instead of sagging in the middle, which is the most common failure point on wider sofas built with cheaper foam.</p>
<h2>Designs Available in This Collection</h2>
<p>This range includes curved and boucle 4 seater sofas for contemporary living rooms, channel tufted and velvet designs for more formal spaces, and L shape 4 seater layouts for corner placement. Several designs in this collection also work well as the basis for a larger 6 seater or 8 seater arrangement, paired with a matching 2 seater or armchairs from elsewhere in our range, if your room calls for more total seating than one piece provides.</p>
<p>Dimensions vary noticeably across designs in this size. A 4 seater sofa with low arms and a curved silhouette will read differently in a room than one with a tall tufted back and square arms, even at similar widths. Each product page lists the full dimensions so you can check the fit against your room before ordering, since a piece this size is harder to reposition once it is in the house.</p>
<h2>Fabric and Frame Choices</h2>
<p>Boucle and chenille are the most requested fabrics for 4 seater sofas in this collection, holding up well against daily use and Lahore''s dustier months without showing wear quickly. Velvet is available for buyers who want a more formal look, particularly on channel tufted designs, though it benefits from occasional brushing to keep the pile looking fresh. If you are choosing between fabrics for a piece this size, message us on WhatsApp with a photo of your room and we can suggest what tends to work best.</p>
<h2>Who a 4 Seater Sofa Suits Best</h2>
<p>A 4 seater sofa works particularly well for households that want generous seating without the complexity of a sectional, or for living rooms with one long uninterrupted wall rather than a corner to build an L shape around. It also suits buyers who find a standard 3 seater slightly short for their family but do not want the visual weight of a full 6 or 7 seater set dominating the room. Because this size sits between two more commonly searched categories, it often ends up being the better fit for a specific room even when buyers start out looking at 3 seater or 5 seater options instead.</p>
<h2>How to Order</h2>
<p>Choose your design and confirm the fabric colour with us directly over WhatsApp. We begin production once 60 percent of the price is paid in advance, with the remaining 40 percent due before dispatch. A 4 seater sofa typically takes 20 to 25 working days to craft and deliver from our Lahore workshop, and delivery is available across Pakistan, not limited to Lahore alone.</p>
<p>Because a 4 seater sofa occupies more wall and floor space than a standard 3 seater, measuring your room before ordering is worth doing properly. Send us your dimensions if you want a second opinion before you commit to a design.</p>'
WHERE slug = '/seater-sofas/4-seater-sofas/' OR name ILIKE '4 Seater%';

UPDATE categories
SET content_html = '<h2>5 Seater Sofa Collection</h2>
<p>A 5 seater sofa set is one of the most searched furniture categories in Pakistan, and for good reason. It is the default scale for a Pakistani drawing room built around hosting, whether that means weekly family visits, Eid gatherings, or a wedding season where the sitting room needs to hold more people than usual. This collection is built specifically for that scale: every 5 seater sofa here is made to order at our workshop in Lahore, designed to anchor a room rather than just fill it.</p>
<h2>What a 5 Seater Sofa Set Actually Needs to Do</h2>
<p>A 5 seater sofa price in Pakistan is usually compared on fabric and finish first, but the part that determines whether the set still looks and feels right in five years is underneath the upholstery. Every piece in this collection is built on a solid wood frame with a 2.5-year warranty, which matters more at this size than on smaller sofas, since a wider frame under more regular weight is where joints loosen first if the construction is weak. The cushioning throughout uses Molty Foam, backed by a 5-year warranty, holding its shape across long seat runs instead of dipping in the centre after a year of use.</p>
<p>This collection includes both single-piece 5 seater sofas and sectional layouts, including curved, L shape, and U shape designs. A curved or crescent-shaped 5 seater suits open living rooms where guests face inward toward each other, while an L shape design works better against two walls in a more traditional layout. If your household leans toward formal seating arrangements, look at the channel tufted and boucle sofa sets in this collection, several of which are designed as a complete suite with matching armchairs rather than a single sofa alone.</p>
<h2>Sizing and Layout for a 5 Seater Sofa</h2>
<p>A 5 seater sofa design in Pakistan typically follows one of two layouts: a continuous long sofa, or a 3 1 1 configuration combining a 3 seater with two single armchairs. Both appear in this collection, and the right choice depends on how your room is shaped. A continuous 5 seater works better along one long wall, while a 3 1 1 set gives you more flexibility to angle the pieces around a coffee table or rearrange them for different gatherings.</p>
<p>Dimensions matter more at this scale than on any smaller sofa, since a 5 seater that is even slightly oversized for a room can make the space feel cramped rather than generous. Every product page in this collection lists the full dimensions, including total width for sectional and curved pieces, so you can check the footprint against your room before ordering.</p>
<h2>Fabric and Finish Across the Collection</h2>
<p>Boucle is the most requested finish in this collection, holding its texture well and suiting both contemporary and warmer traditional interiors. Velvet appears across several channel tufted and Chesterfield-leaning designs for buyers who want a more formal drawing room centrepiece, while a smaller number of pieces use corduroy or linen-blend fabric for a more relaxed, everyday character. If you are ordering for a room that sees daily use rather than occasional formal seating, we typically recommend boucle or a performance fabric over velvet, since it holds up better against regular contact.</p>
<h2>Ordering a 5 Seater Sofa from ComfyClub</h2>
<p>Confirm your design and fabric colour with us over WhatsApp, where we can also help you decide between a continuous sofa and a sectional or 3 1 1 layout based on your room. Production begins once 60 percent of the price is paid in advance, with the remaining 40 percent due before delivery. A 5 seater sofa typically takes 25 to 30 working days to craft and deliver from our Lahore workshop, slightly longer than smaller pieces given the scale of the build, and we deliver across Pakistan including Karachi, Islamabad, and Rawalpindi, not only within Lahore.</p>
<p>If you are unsure whether a continuous 5 seater or a sectional layout fits your room better, send us your dimensions before ordering and we will recommend the configuration that makes the most sense for the space.</p>'
WHERE slug = '/seater-sofas/5-seater-sofas/' OR name ILIKE '5 Seater%';

SELECT name, slug, length(content_html) AS content_chars
FROM categories
WHERE slug IN ('/seater-sofas/3-seater-sofas/', '/seater-sofas/4-seater-sofas/', '/seater-sofas/5-seater-sofas/')
ORDER BY slug;
